16.2(7)(A) (A) document the medication error in the Person's medical data sheet;
16.2(7)(B) (B) determine if a critical incident report needs to be submitted;
16.2(7)(C) (C) notify the Person's Support Coordinator in writing within one Calendar Day;
16.2(7)(D) (D) assess the need for a written Remediation Plan to minimize the reoccurrence of the error and develop a plan if needed. If a plan exists, the PM1 Staff shall assess the adequacy of the plan and revise the plan as needed;
16.2(7)(E) (E) document the medication error and Remediation Plan (if needed) in the Person's medical data sheet; and
16.2(7)(F) (F) If the PM1 Staff becomes aware of a medication error on the day of the error, assess the Person's health risk as a result of the error, and if other providers of services to the Person need to be notified. If the medication error was on a prior date, the PM1 Staff shall notify the Contractor's director or designee where the error occurred.

16.2(9)(A) (A) is based on data the PM1 Staff has collected through observation, discussion with other Staff providing services to the Person, review of records of other services the Person is receiving, and direct examination of the Person;
16.2(9)(B) (B) includes the following: (i) safety and efficacy of the Person's prescribed medication within the PM1 Staff's scope of practice and training; (ii) demonstrable benefits (or lack thereof) the Person has from their medication regimen; (iii) any adverse medication reactions or side effects the Person is experiencing; (iv) the Person's adherence or lack of adherence with their health care professional's medication related orders; and (v) any barriers to adherence to health care professional's medication related orders that the PM1 Staff identifies;
16.2(9)(C) (C) results are documented in a note in the Person's medical data sheet. The PM1 Staff must include the following in the documentation:
16.2(9)(C)(i) (i) a description of the Person's subjective presentation; (ii) a description of the PM1 Staff's objective observations after the examination, including a review of records and consultations with other Staff providing other services or supports to the Person or the Person's family/representative; (iii) a description of the Person's status made by the PM1 Staff of the; and (iv) a plan for the Person's continuing care surrounding their health status and medication regimen.
16.2(9)(D) (D) includes any notes, any known allergies the Person has, any medication errors that occur, and any written Remediation Plans to minimize the reoccurrence of each medication error if an error has occurred.

17.2(7)(A) (A) document the medication error in the Person's medical data sheet;
17.2(7)(B) (B) determine if a critical incident report needs to be submitted;
17.2(7)(C) (C) notify the Person's Support Coordinator in writing within one Calendar Day;
17.2(7)(D) (D) assess the need for a written Corrective Action Plan to minimize the reoccurrence of the error and develop a plan if needed. If a plan exists, the PM2 Staff shall assess the adequacy of the plan and revise the plan as needed;
17.2(7)(E) (E) document the medication error and Corrective Action Plan (if needed) in the Person's medical data sheet; and
17.2(7)(F) (F) If the PM2 Staff becomes aware of a medication error on the day of the error, assess the Person's health risk as a result of the error, and if other providers of services to the Person need to be notified. If the medication error was on a prior date, the PM2 Staff shall notify the Contractor's director or designee where the error occurred.

17.2(9)(A) (A) is based on data the PM2 Staff has collected through observation, discussion with other Staff providing services to the Person, review of records of other services the Person is receiving, and direct examination of the Person;
17.2(9)(B) (B) includes the following: (i) safety and efficacy of the Person's prescribed medication within the PM2 Staff's scope of practice and training; (ii) benefits that the Person is demonstrating as a result of their medication regimen, or the lack thereof; (iii) any adverse medication reactions or side effects that the Person is experiencing; (iv) the Person's adherence or lack of adherence with their health care professional's medication related orders; and (v) any barriers to adherence to health care professional's medication related orders that the PM2 Staff identifies;
17.2(9)(C) (C) results are documented in a note in the Person's medical data sheet. The PM2 Staff shall include in the documentation the following:
17.2(9)(C)(i) (i) a description of the Person's subjective presentation; (ii) a description of the objective observations the PM2 Staff has made after the examination, including a review of records and consultations with other Staff providing other services or supports to the Person or the Person's family/representative; (iii) a description of the assessment made by the PM2 Staff of the Person's status; and (iv) a plan for the continuing care of the Person surrounding their health status and medication regimen.
17.2(9)(D) (D) includes any notes, any known allergies the Person has, any medication errors that occur, and any written corrective action plans to minimize the reoccurrence of each medication error if an error has occurred.

18.3(2)(A) (A) the name of the service provided (PN1);
18.3(2)(B) (B) the service delivery date;
18.3(2)(C) (C) the name of Person receiving the service;
18.3(2)(D) (D) the name of the Staff providing the service; and
18.3(2)(E) (E) a general summary daily note or shift summary of goals worked on and progress made completed by a Staff that provided the service. The summary should tie back to the Person's PSCP or support strategies and/or be consistent with the service description.

19.2(1)(A) (A) hands-on care of G-tubes, urinary catheters, colostomy bags, and other similar medical devices;
19.2(1)(C) (C) sterile procedures or processes, invasive procedures, injectable medication administration, central line maintenance, and other similar services requiring nursing judgment; and
19.2(1)(D) (D) medication management services, medication monitoring, and medication and medical equipment education and training as outlined in DHHS service codes PM1 and PM2.

19.2(7)(A) (A) the Person's name, medical condition, current medications, and explanation of medical care needed;
19.2(7)(B) (B) specific details on the delegated tasks, including what the tasks are and how to successfully complete the tasks;
19.2(7)(C) (C) specific details on adverse reactions the Staff (who the service is being delegated to) must be aware of, and how and when such reactions need be reported to the RN PN2 Staff;
19.2(7)(D) (D) how often the Staff (who the services are being delegated to) must meet with the RN PN2 Staff to coordinate the Person's medical care needs. At a minimum, they must meet monthly; and
19.2(7)(E) (E) how often the Staff (who services are delegated to) must submit a report summarizing the Person's services, to the RN PN2 Staff. At a minimum, a report must be submitted monthly.
